# One owner, because there is one maintainer.
# A second reviewer is the goal, not the current state -- this file exists so
# that "who signs off" is written down rather than implied. When a CODEOWNERS
# entry names only an unavailable owner, GitHub still requests the review; it
# does not let the PR self-approve silently.
#
# See SECURITY.md for the vulnerability route, which is a GitHub Security
# Advisory and deliberately does not go through a public PR.
*       @Sanflow10

# Anything that decides whether a patch merges is the highest-risk surface in
# this repository: a defect here fails open, on someone else's code, in their
# CI. These need review even when nothing else does.
/src/core/gate.py        @Sanflow10
/src/verifiers/          @Sanflow10
/src/cli.py              @Sanflow10
/action.yml              @Sanflow10

# The file that actually spawns the code under test.
/src/sandbox/runner.py   @Sanflow10

# CI is the only thing currently attesting to any of the above.
/.github/workflows/      @Sanflow10
